{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547610-under-the-mountain-the-jadeborn","id":1547610,"title":"Under the Mountain: The Jadeborn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-06T20:18:48-08:00","id":1547610,"title":"Under the Mountain: The Jadeborn","content":"<i>Excerpts from a back-burner project I've had going for a while. Still very much WIP, and I keep changing my mind about the mechanics. But I think there's still something interesting just in the approach to the lore, so sharing some bits here.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Under the Mountain</b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sidebar: What are Mountain Folk?</b><br /> <br /> Mountain Folk are Tolkien\u2019s Elves, if instead of retreating West when their Age ended they were instead metaphysically lobotomized and literally forced underground. Though they do not remember it, their souls are older than the world they have been stranded in. Before the Geas, they represented a legitimate competitor to the humans of Creation.<br /> <br /> What they are <i>not</i> is Exalted. Like Tolkien\u2019s Elves and Dwarfs, they are blessed with exceptional physiques, and the Enlightened with brilliant minds, but their magic is something harnessed and shaped rather than coming from their indomitable spirit.<br /> <br /> First, start with the ecology of the MF. They\u2019re not mushroom farmers - they\u2019re cultivating Demesnes so they can harvest essence (dweomer). MF are not mortals - they\u2019re alien exiles from another dimension. They need essence-rich materials, both for sustenance and their crafting/maintenance. End result - Artisans are playing an RTS against the Endless Hordes.<br /> <br /> Consistent with their alienness, they are also an excuse to bring in some European mythological influences that the setting typically avoids. Gaelic, Norse, Germanic, Latin, Greek. </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Graces Trapped in Amber</b></span><br /> <br /> Of the nigh-infinite Unshaped in the vicinity of the catastrophic collapse of possibility that birthed Creation, almost all were simply obliterated. A few, sensing what was happening, reflexively retreated through the Gateway of Sundraprisha even as it formed, becoming the first noble raksha. For most this was merely a brief stay of execution. Stranded in a hostile new world, with no context from which to craft Assumptions and no mortals yet invented upon which to feed, they quickly succumbed to calcification and dissolution.<br /> <br /> A lucky few nobles of the Ring, with the strong sense of self-awareness reflected in that Grace and the good fortune to take Shape deep underground, were entombed in cysts of jade by the generative powers unleashed in that moment. Such were the uncountable numbers of the Unshaped in the Before that even this fraction of a fraction of a fraction of that group yet numbered in the millions, concentrated in the center of Creation, deep under Meru the Omphalos, now called the Imperial Mountain. These would one day become the Jadeborn.<br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Enlightened - Ascendent Ring</b></span><br /> <br /> The comparatively rare Enlightened are cousins to those raksha nobles with an ascendent Ring, for whom personal ambition is the defining characteristic. This preeminence of self enables a greater capacity for self-improvement; common to all Enlightened is their need to follow their own muse. They also find it easier for learn Patterns associated with other Castes.<br /> <br /> When Mountain Folk souls first crystalized out of raksha essence, only those newborn nobles sheltered by ascendent Ring Graces survived the process - the first generation of Mountain Folk were thus all Enlightened. Hatching the Jade Egg is not able to lift the Geas, but can repair some of the damage in a few cases. All Artisans are thus Enlightened, along with a small fraction of Workers and Warriors.<br /> <br /> <b>Artisans (FKA Panjandrums - Shadowed Staff - Community serving Self)</b><br /> <br /> Artisans make the great project that is Mountain Folk society itself their primary focus. In influencing the Conclave, maintaining the economy, and operating the logistics of the Endless War, they leave their mark on on their world.<br /> <br /> <b>Enlightened Workers (FKA Artisans - Shadowed Cup - Desirability serving Self)</b><br /> <br /> Enlightened Workers are often eccentric crafters of wonders. Their greatest works almost always have a civically-minded purpose, because above all else they want their creations to be appreciated long after their passing.<br /> <br /> <b>Enlightened Warriors (FKA Strategos - Shadowed Sword - Conflict serving Self)</b><br /> <br /> The projects of Enlightened Workers are cornerstones of the Endless War - Campaigns to take or retake territory from the Endless Hordes, or the fortifications and formations that resist the inevitable counteroffensives are their highest form of creativity.<br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u200b<b>Undercastes - Shadowed Ring</b></span><br /> <br /> The Undercastes are cousins to those raksha patterns with shadowed Rings; those who find their purpose in the functionary\u2019s life and service to greater causes. The Undercastes are a tangible manifestation of the spiritual damage inflicted on the Jadeborn by the Great Geas.<br /> <br /> Every member of the Undercastes has a least one Major or Defining Tie to their society or species of an appropriate positive context. Influence that would erode their last such Intimacy below Major is treated as Unacceptable.<br /> <br /> <b>Workers (Ascendent Cup)</b><br /> <br /> The arts of the Cup are those of making oneself <i>useful</i>. The wants and needs of others give Ornamental Raksha their purpose, but unlike in the Wyld, in Creation needs are very material. Food to eat, water to drink, shelter in which to find safety. Providing these for their people is the calling of the Worker caste.<br /> <br /> <b>Warriors (Ascendent Sword)</b><br /> <br /> The Warriors are born of patterns that among the raksha would be Cataphracts; those who fight in service to a greater cause. A Warrior\u2019s purpose is conflict - in a world of finite resources, their contribution to society is to seize and defend the means of production, without which society could not exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sidebar: The Missing Caste</b><br /> <br /> In the connection to primeval Raksha and their Graces, one gap stands out: Scribes, the raksha of ascendant Staff and shadowed Ring, functionaries and cogs of the machine of state. Worker assistants to the Artisan Caste fill this niche, but it is the nature of these attendants to serve the idiosyncratic needs of their immediate superiors rather than the community as a whole. It is difficult to look at the state of Mountain Folk society and wonder how things might be different were the willfull, self-interested politicians of the Conclave surrounded by a class of <i>public</i> servants rather than <i>personal</i> servants.<br /> <br /> So what happened to the original Artisans broken and inverted by the Great Geas? Certainly Artisans are more common than the other two varieties of Enlightened. Perhaps the same Artisan conspiracy that has suppressed the true nature of the Enlightened Undercastes has hidden knowledge of these as well; the jade nodules hosting such spirits tithed to the Second Deliberative long ago, to be minted into reinforcement for the Order-Conferring Trade Pattern. Perhaps Hatching the Jade Egg is more reliable for souls with Staff patterns, and the few Ascendent Staff souls were all reincarnated as Artisans within a generation.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-07T11:30:32-08:00","id":1547619,"title":"","content":"Certainly does way more with their Fair Folk origins than their traditional portrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-07T19:40:56-08:00","id":1547625,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it always bugged me that Artisans (the name of a type of Worker noble) were more like Raksha Diplomats, and their were no Entertainers. But the more I picked it apart, the more I thought maybe that was deliberate obfuscation by the author (Jenna Moran I think? And it seems like something she'd do). Worker MFs are motivated above all else by being useful and valued; you see it in their Charmset as subservience-based abilities, which is very Cup. And the Ring is fundamentally about identity and self, which manifests in certain types of crafting in the Wyld, but it's not about Craft in general - the closest analogs to Hatching the Jade Egg are all in Staff for instance. The whole idea just kind of flowed organically from there. Note this is easier to see in 1st Edition; the Patterns were an unbalanced mess just like FF, but they were internally coherent in away 2e lacked (which happened again with Sidereals; same original author).<br /> <br /> That said, beyond all this foundational metaphysics, this division shows up in which Charms appear in which Patterns and the like, but the connection to the Raksha doesn't really show up more in their day-to-day life, which I see as being largely like the canon Jadeborn (though with less magitech).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-07-2025, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-08T05:57:01-08:00","id":1547632,"title":"","content":"I believe the first edition version of Mountain Folk was done by Neph but I'm unclear who exactly did what in that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T19:45:40-08:00","id":1547838,"title":"","content":"Idle thought - Autocthon hatched the Mountain Folk, but it was the divine ignition, Cytherea, that burned through the Wyld and collapsed infinite potential to solid actuality. I wonder if there is anything to be made from Cytherea as the mother of the Jadeborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}